# AGENTS.md — Instructions for Coding Agents

Copy to repo root as `AGENTS.md` and fill the `{{...}}` placeholders.
This is the **lite** adoption tier: enough for a coding agent without copying the full Agentix loop.

## Project Goal

{{ONE_SENTENCE_GOAL}}

## Current Status

{{STATUS_ONE_LINER}}

## Recommended Stack (do not deviate without an ADR)

- Language / runtime: {{STACK}}
- Package manager: {{PKG}}
- Tests: {{TEST_CMD}}
- Lint / types: {{LINT_CMD}}

## Exact Commands

```bash
{{INSTALL_CMD}}
{{LINT_CMD}}
{{TEST_CMD}}
{{RUN_CMD}}
```

## Definition of Done (any feature)

- [ ] Types / schemas updated at the single source of truth (no parallel interfaces)
- [ ] Tests for the change (fixture or unit); existing suite still green
- [ ] Docs / mapping table updated when the data shape changes
- [ ] No secrets, tokens, real user IDs, or raw PII committed
- [ ] One logical change per PR; conventional commit

## Boundaries — NEVER

- Commit `.env`, tokens, private keys, or live personal data
- Invent a second source of truth for types or domain objects
- Skip the exact commands above in favor of an improvised toolchain
- Mix unrelated concerns (parser + UI restyle, schema + drive-by refactors)

## Preferred Development Loop

1. Read this file + the spec / domain doc named in `{{SPEC_FILE}}`
2. Smallest vertical slice that meets the next acceptance criterion
3. Write or update tests first when behavior changes
4. Run the exact lint + test commands
5. Commit as a human mid/senior developer (see DEVELOPMENT_STANDARDS if the full loop is wired)

## When to upgrade to the full Agentix loop

Use `Agent-Init.consumer.sh` + `prompts/short_orchestrator_prompt.md` when you need
autonomous multi-cycle work (O→C→T→D→R), not for a one-shot product PR.

See `examples/consumer-starter/README.md`.
